    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix",
    "problem": "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=[\\begin{aligned}9-7\\text{i} & -2\\text{i} & 6-\\text{i} \\\\ -7 & 5-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 6 & -\\text{i} & 0\\end{aligned}].$ What is the value of ${b}_{21}+{b}_{32}?$",
    "worked_solution": "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}9-7\\text{i} & -2\\text{i} & 6-\\text{i} \\\\ -7 & 5-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 6 & -\\text{i} & 0\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{9-7\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-7} & \\overset{―}{5-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{6} & \\overset{―}{-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{0}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9+7\\text{i} & 2\\text{i} & 6+\\text{i} \\\\ -7 & 5+\\text{i} & -\\text{i} \\\\ 6 & \\text{i} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{21}+{b}_{32}=-7+\\text{i}.$",
